==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|lane}}, {{m|enm|lone}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lanu||a lane, alley, avenue}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*lanu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*lanō||lane, passageway}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|lone||cattle-track, by-road}}, {{cog|fy|leane}}, {{m|fy|loane||a walkway, avenue}}, {{cog|nl|laan||alley, avenue}}, {{cog|nds-de|Lane}}, {{m|nds-de|Laan|t=lane}}, {{cog|sv|lån||covered walkway encircling a house}}, {{cog|is|lön||a row of houses}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/leɪn/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-lane.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪn|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|lain}}
<!-- 1 syllable words !-->

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|used in street names}} A [[road]], [[street]], or similar [[thoroughfare]].
#: {{ux|en|Penny '''Lane'''}}
# A [[narrow]] [[passageway]] between [[fence]]s, [[wall]]s, [[hedge]]s or [[tree]]s.
#: {{ux|en|There's a shortcut to the shops through this leafy '''lane'''.}}
# A narrow road, as in the [[country]].
# A lengthwise division of [[roadway]] intended for a single line of [[vehicle]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Drivers should overtake in the outside '''lane'''}}
#: {{ux|en|We were held up by a truck in the middle '''lane''' of the freeway.}}
#: {{ux|en|the exit '''lane'''}}
# {{lb|en|athletics}} A similar division of a [[racetrack]] to keep [[runner]]s apart.
#: {{ux|en|There are eight '''lanes''' on an Olympic running track.}}
# {{lb|en|swimming}} A similar division of a [[swimming pool]] using lines of coloured floats to keep [[swimmer]]s apart.
#: {{ux|en|a swimming '''lane'''}}
# Any of a number of parallel tracks or passages.
#: {{ux|en|the checkout '''lanes''' in a supermarket}}
# A [[course]] designated for [[ship]]s or [[aircraft]].
#: {{ux|en|shipping '''lane'''}}
# {{lb|en|bowling}} An elongated wooden strip of floor along which a [[bowling ball]] is rolled.
#: {{ux|en|We booked a couple of '''lanes''' at the bowling alley.}}
# {{lb|en|card games}} An empty space in the [[tableau]], formed by the removal of an entire row of cards.
# {{lb|en|computing}} Any of the [[parallel]] [[slot]]s in which [[value]]s can be stored in a [[SIMD]] [[architecture]].
# {{lb|en|video games}} In [[MOBA]] ([[multiplayer]] [[online]] [[battle]] [[arena]]) games, a particular [[path]] on the [[map]] that may be traversed by enemy characters.
# {{lb|en|horse racing}} The [[home stretch]].
#: {{ux|en|And it's Uncle Mo in front by two as they come to the top of the '''lane'''.}}

