==Middle English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|enm|lone}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|enm|ang|lanu}}, from {{inh|enm|gmw-pro|*lanu}}, from {{inh|enm|gem-pro|*lanō}}.

The form {{m|enm|lone}} continues Mercian {{m+|ang|lone}}, reflecting the dialectal rounding of Germanic *{{IPAchar|/ɑn/}}. In most words, this rounding is only apparent in Western Middle English, but ''lone'' is the usual Northern form as well, making it a relic of the wider Old English distribution.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|enm|/ˈlaːn(ə)/}}
* {{IPA|enm|/ˈlɔːn(ə)/|/ˈlɒːn(ə)/|a=West Midland, Northern}}

===Noun===
{{enm-noun}}

# {{l|en|lane}}, [[alley]] {{gloss|narrow [[passage]] between buildings}}
# {{lb|enm|by extension}} Any [[road]] or [[street]].
# {{lb|enm|rare}} A [[path]] or [[track]].

